Path: `cmd/entire/cli/understand_build.go`.\n\n- Orchestrates scan → structural index → history fuse → semantic → timeline → manifest write, with `errgroup` parallelism for independent stages.\n- Flags: `--full`, `--provider`, `--model`, `--concurrency`, `--no-semantic` for CI.\n- Resolves provider via the existing summary-generation path; if no provider available, marks semantic stage `skipped` in `manifest.json` and continues.\n- Persists manifest fingerprint (repo HEAD sha + checkpoints/v1 head sha + supported langs) so future incremental builds can detect drift.\n- Tests via `testutil.InitRepo` for: build with no checkpoints, build with checkpoints, semantic skipped path, manifest fingerprint stability, parallel-stage cancellation.\n- Commit: `understand: build command pipeline`.\n\n### 4. `explain` primitive (~300 LOC + tests)\nPath: `cmd/entire/cli/understand_explain.go`.\n\n- Resolves a file path or exact node ID, returns structural identity + owning domain/pattern + most recent checkpoint trail + transcript references.\n- Honors the `scope:symbol` vs `scope:file-owner` rendering rule — mixed strings forbidden.\n- CLI markdown by default, `--json` shape stable for downstream commands.\n- Tests for path normalization, missing-cache hint, scope rendering distinction, missing-node error.\n- Commit: `understand: explain primitive`.\n\n### 5. `tour` / `impact` / `examples` / `hotspots` (~1000 LOC + tests)\n- `understand_tour.go`: resolves area, picks compact subgraph, calls semantic narration if available.\n- `understand_impact.go`: dependency walk + deterministic conflict hints + optional agent wording.\n- `understand_examples.go`: parse pattern as data, lexical + graph-shape + domain-node match.\n- `understand_hotspots.go`: scoring from checkpoint count, distinct-agent count, churn, centrality, contradiction flags.\n- All four ship CLI text + `--json` and the deterministic fallback on missing semantic.\n- Commit: `understand: tour/impact/examples/hotspots`.\n\n### 6. `pr` command (~300 LOC + tests)\nPath: `cmd/entire/cli/understand_pr.go`.\n\n- Numeric PR lookup via `gh pr view --json` when on PATH; fall back to `--base`/`--head` or revset.\n- Never reads or writes credentials; defers all auth to user's `gh`.\n- Tests for `gh` missing, `gh` failure, manual base/head fallback, JSON output shape.\n- Commit: `understand: pr review brief`.\n\n### 7. `prime` command (~300 LOC + tests)\nPath: `cmd/entire/cli/understand_prime.go`.\n\n- Default mode prints/copies a bounded markdown or JSON priming packet.\n- `--exec --agent claude-code` invokes the existing claude-code integration; other agent names produce a clear \"not yet supported for --exec\" message — no arbitrary `--` passthrough.\n- Tests: default packet shape, `--exec` claude-code happy path, unsupported-agent message.\n- Commit: `understand: prime command`.\n\n### 8. `dashboard` + `replay` (~1500–2000 LOC + tests)\nPaths: `cmd/entire/cli/understand_dashboard.go`, `understand_replay.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/understand/dashboard/` (Go server + assets).\n\n- Bind 127.0.0.1, ephemeral random bearer token per launch, header-only auth (never query string), read-only endpoints, never bulk-expose transcripts. Prompt bodies fetched on demand by checkpoint ID.\n- Vanilla HTML/CSS/JavaScript via `go:embed` (mirrors `dispatch/voices.go` pattern). One off-the-shelf graph renderer (cytoscape.js or vis-network) loaded as a static asset; license + version recorded in the PR. No node toolchain.\n- Tests: token enforcement, read-only contract, bulk-transcript-exposure regression, replay scrubber JSON.\n- This is the single biggest chunk in the spec. If asset size or LOC pushes the diff past reviewable, I will pause and re-raise per the spec's escape hatch rather than silently splitting.\n- Commit: `understand: dashboard + replay`.\n\n### 9. Integration tests + `.gitignore` docs (~500 LOC + docs)\nPath: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/understand_*_test.go`.\n\n- End-to-end: `build` → `status`