{"parentUuid":"b0d2b026-a47b-4909-b64b-41dd83f2f3d4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015x56PYRXZLMK3799eWeW5s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Honest answer: probably not for this POC, yes worth considering as a future backend.**\n\nWhat graphiti actually is (verified just now): Python-only, requires Python 3.10+, a graph DB (Neo4j / FalkorDB / Kuzu / Neptune), and an LLM provider for entity/relationship extraction. **No Go SDK** — the only way to use it from this repo would be a sidecar process (REST or MCP), the same pattern marvin already uses for its memory store.\n\nHow that lines up with the spec we're implementing:\n\n| Spec constraint | Native Go (current plan) | Graphiti |\n|---|---|---|\n| \"no new Go module dependencies for the core engine\" | clean | adds Python + Docker + graph DB runtime |\n| \"no remote service dependency for core queries\" | clean | introduces a sidecar service, even if local |\n| \"native Entire-owned implementation\" (rejected `Wrap`) | matches the chosen Fuse architecture | revives a `Wrap`-style dependency on an external graph engine |\n| \"single-PR POC, .entire/understand/ as local cache\" | matches | mismatched — wants long-lived stateful service |\n| \"do not duplicate raw prompt content into graph artifacts\" | trivially clean (we store IDs only) | harder — graphiti's pull is LLM-extracted facts, which means feeding prompt content through an LLM during ingest |\n\nWhere graphiti actually shines and is genuinely tempting:\n1. **Bi-temporal queries** — \"what did we believe about this code on date X\" maps well to moment 6 (replay).\n2. **LLM-assisted entity extraction** from transcripts/prompts — overlaps with our semantic stage.\n3. **Mature schema for evolving facts** — saves us reinventing churn/superseded-fact logic.\n\nBut the cost is real: it would push the CLI from \"Go binary that writes JSON files\" to \"Go binary that orchestrates Docker + Python + graph DB\" — and the spec's chosen-architecture decision in marvin memory explicitly says \"native Entire-owned implementation, do not use Understand-Anything\", which is the same shape of tradeoff.\n\n**My recommendation:** keep the plan as-is for the single-PR POC. Build the native graph + JSON store, use agent CLIs for bounded synthesis. If the feature graduates beyond POC and we need bi-temporal queries or richer fact extraction, swapping the storage layer to a graphiti-backed service is a much smaller migration than baking it in at v1 — the `graph.Store` interface I already have is the natural seam.\n\nWant me to:\n\n**(a)** Keep the plan as-is and proceed with native implementation,\n**(b)** Revise the plan to use graphiti as the storage backend (would push us into multi-PR territory; needs reviewer sign-off on the dependency posture change),\n**(c)** Take a hybrid path — native JSON store now but design the `graph.Store` interface to be cleanly swappable to graphiti later (small additions to plan), or\n**(d)** Pause the implementation entirely and produce a separate ADR comparing graphiti vs native before continuing?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":631,"cache_read_input_tokens":198327,"output_tokens":1250,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":631,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1250,"cache_read_input_tokens":198327,"cache_creation_input_tokens":631,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":631},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CajttR9rEpKKPvWoxkeg6","type":"assistant","uuid":"ce6d3ee6-e0fe-4c86-8931-1b6ee7ae8dcf","timestamp":"2026-05-05T18:28:55.679Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/alisha/.marvi