{"parentUuid":"75a74768-0d24-46b1-8564-441354793431","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/collab-95042499-claude/cmd/entire/cli/understand_prime.go","snippet":"1\tpackage cli\n2\t\n3\timport (\n4\t\t\"context\"\n5\t\t\"errors\"\n6\t\t\"fmt\"\n7\t\t\"io\"\n8\t\t\"os\"\n9\t\t\"os/exec\"\n10\t\t\"sort\"\n11\t\t\"strings\"\n12\t\n13\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/jsonutil\"\n14\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/understand/graph\"\n15\t\t\"github.com/spf13/cobra\"\n16\t)\n17\t\n18\t// newUnderstandPrimeCmd builds `entire understand prime [<path>...]`.\n19\t//\n20\t// Default behavior prints a bounded markdown priming packet to stdout (or\n21\t// JSON via --json). With --exec --agent <name> the packet is piped into\n22\t// the agent's interactive CLI as the first user message.\n23\t//\n24\t// Per the spec: this command is explicit, never runs in hooks, and the POC\n25\t// ships --exec support for claude-code only. Other agents are accepted but\n26\t// return a clear \"not yet supported for --exec\" message rather than silently\n27\t// printing the packet.\n28\tfunc newUnderstandPrimeCmd() *cobra.Command {\n29\t\tvar (\n30\t\t\tjsonOut     bool\n31\t\t\texecMode    bool\n32\t\t\tagentName   string\n33\t\t\ttopHotspots int\n34\t\t)\n35\t\n36\t\tcmd := &cobra.Command{\n37\t\t\tUse:   \"prime [<path>...]\",\n38\t\t\tShort: \"Generate a priming packet for the next agent session\",\n39\t\t\tLong: `Build a structural + historical priming packet to orient an agent at the\n40\tstart of a new session.\n41\t\n42\tModes:\n43\t  default        Print the markdown packet to stdout (use --json for machine output).\n44\t  --exec --agent claude-code\n45\t                 Launch the agent's CLI with the packet piped as stdin. Other\n46\t                 agents are accepted by name but produce a \"not yet supported\"\n47\t                 message rather than silently exec'ing.\n48\t\n49\tExamples:\n50\t