n173\t\n174\tThat preserves the requested “hover to know why / click for transcript” user\n175\tmoment without creating a second unbounded store of sensitive prompt content.\n176\t\n177\t### Checkpoint-to-node relationship: checkpoints are first-class nodes\n178\t\n179\tFor the native Entire version, checkpoints should be **nodes**, not just\n180\tattributes.\n181\t\n182\tWhy:\n183\t\n184\t- moments 2, 3, 5, 6, 7, and 8 all ask history questions that become awkward if\n185\t  checkpoints are only embedded blobs on file nodes\n186\t- replay/time-slider naturally wants a time-ordered event graph\n187\t- examples/hotspots/priming benefit from traversing from symbols or domains to\n188\t  the concrete checkpoints that established them\n189\t\n190\tAttribution rules stay honest:\n191\t\n192\t- **File-level evidence is authoritative** via `FilesTouched`\n193\t  (`checkpoint/checkpoint.go`, `session/state.go`).\n194\t- **Symbol-level edges are deterministic only when evidence exists**, such as:\n195\t  - diff hunk overlap with symbol line ranges\n196\t  - tool telemetry/file paths plus line references when available\n197\t  - symbol introduction/removal observed while rebuilding timeline snapshots\n198\t- If symbol precision is unavailable, Entire links checkpoint → file and marks\n199\t  any symbol association as `scope:file-owner` rather than presenting it as\n200\t  proven symbol-level authorship.\n201\t- **User-facing honesty**: CLI and dashboard rendering MUST distinguish\n202\t  `scope:symbol` evidence from `scope:file-owner` inference. Inferred associations\n203\t  render with a clear \"(file-level inferred)\" qualifier; deterministic ones do\n204\t  not. The implementation MUST NOT emit a single rendered string that conflates\n205\t  the two scopes.\n206\t\n207\t### Build pipeline: deterministic first, agent-assisted second\n208\t\n209\t`entire understand build` is explicit and owns the full pipeline.\n210\t\n211\tPipeline stages:\n212\t\n213\t1. **Scan**\n214\t   - enumerate repo files from repo root\n215\t   - classify language and file category\n216\t   - exclude `.git/`, `.entire/understand/`, agent-owned protected dirs, and\n217\t     other generated state\n218\t\n219\t2. **Structural index**\n220\t   - build file/package/module/symbol/import/call/reference data\n221\t   - **POC parser coverage (pinned to keep single-PR scope honest):**\n222\t     - Go: full symbol extraction via `go/parser` + `go/types` (stdlib only —\n223\t       no new module dependencies)\n224\t     - all other languages: file-level nodes only (path, language guess from\n225\t       extension, size, last-touched checkpoint)\n226\t   - tree-sitter / per-language symbol plugins are **explicitly deferred** to a\n227\t     follow-up PR. The graph schema must remain shape-stable so symbol-level\n228\t     data can be added later without rewriting consumers.\n229\t   - the \"every repo file gets a file node\" guarantee holds regardless of\n230\t     language coverage\n231\t\n232\t3. **History fuse**\n233\t   - read checkpoint summaries, metadata, prompts, and `FilesTouched`\n234\t   - create `checkpoint` and `session` nodes\n235\t   - add `touched_in` / `introduced_in` / `modified_in` edges\n236\t   - compute recency, churn, agent diversity, and session counts\n237\t\n238\t4. **Semantic synthesis**\n239\t   - feed bounded, structured graph slices to the user's configured agent using\n240\t     `agent.TextGenerator`\n241\t   - require JSON output for domain graph, pattern graph, tour narration,\n242\t     example explanations, hotspot summaries, and priming packets\n243\t   - never grant the agent direct file-system or tool access during these\n244\t     synthesis calls; Entire owns all retrieval\n245\t   - **Validation and retry posture**: every synthesis call is treated as untrusted\n246\t     output. Entire validates each response against an expected JSON schema; on\n247\t     parse or schema failure it retries once with a stricter \"JSON only, no prose\"\n248\t     reminder, then degrades to deterministic-only output for that shard rather\n249\t     than failing the whole build. All malformed responses are logged via the\n250\t     existing `logging` package (operational metadata only — no raw model output\n251\t     bodies persisted unless `--debug` is set).\n252\t   - **Timeout posture**: every synthesis shard runs under a bounded context\n253\t     deadline. For the POC, reuse the same effective default as\n254\t     `entire explain --generate` (30s per call unless the parent context is\n255\t     already sooner), and degrade that shard on timeout instead of hanging the\n256\t     entire build. Any cross-feature timeout unification is a follow-up.\n257\t   - **Default concurrency**: semantic synthesis runs at a default cap of 3\n258\t     in-flight calls per provider, overridable via `--concurrency` on\n259\t     `entire understand build`. The default is intentionally low because\n260\t     agent-CLI calls are billed and can spawn child processes; users opting into\n261\t     more parallelism is preferable to silently fanning out.\n262\t\n263\t5. **Timeline build**\n264\t   - replay checkpoints/commits in timestamp order\n265\t   - emit graph deltas for introduced/touched/removed nodes and edges\n266\t   - persist view-model-friendly timeline data for replay and dashboard\n267\t\n268\t6. **Materialize caches**\n269\t   - write the local artifact set\n270\t   - compute fingerprints so later builds can run incrementally\n271\t\n272\tParallelism is required throughout:\n273\t\n274\t- file scanning and structural parsing run with `errgroup`/worker pools\n275\t- history fusion batches checkpoint reads where independent\n276\t- semantic synthesis runs per shard in parallel subject to a configurable\n277\t  concurrency cap\n278\t\n279\t### Provider model: reuse the existing summary-generation path\n280\t\n281\tThe feature should use the user's installed agents the same way summary\n282\tgeneration already does.\n283\t