ms full or incremental refresh\n355\t- `entire understand status` reports:\n356\t  - whether artifacts exist\n357\t  - current fingerprint\n358\t  - last build time\n359\t  - checkpoint head seen at build time\n360\t  - provider/model used for semantic stages\n361\t- Commands that rely on stale artifacts warn clearly and offer\n362\t  `entire understand build`\n363\t\n364\t### Dashboard and local API security\n365\t\n366\t`entire understand dashboard` starts a loopback-only local server and opens the\n367\tUI in the browser.\n368\t\n369\tSecurity rules:\n370\t\n371\t- bind to `127.0.0.1` only\n372\t- generate an ephemeral random bearer token per launch\n373\t- require that token on **every** API request\n374\t- never place that token in the URL or query string; keep it in same-origin\n375\t  page bootstrap state / request headers only so it does not leak into browser\n376\t  history, screenshots, or copied links\n377\t- expose read-only endpoints only\n378\t- never expose raw transcript bodies in bulk index endpoints\n379\t- fetch prompt/transcript content on demand by checkpoint ID and only for the\n380\t  active local session token\n381\t\n382\tThis satisfies the repo security rule that all API endpoints require\n383\tauthentication and the most restrictive access by default.\n384\t\n385\t**POC dashboard stack (pinned to avoid scope creep):**\n386\t\n387\t- single-page app served from a Go-side `embed.FS` (the `go:embed` pattern\n388\t  already used in `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/voices.go` and the opencode plugin)\n389\t- vanilla HTML/CSS/JavaScript with one off-the-shelf graph-rendering library\n390\t  (e.g. cytoscape.js or vis-network) loaded statically. No React/Vue/Svelte\n391\t  build step, no transpiler, no node toolchain in this PR.\n392\t- the dashboard binary footprint is part of the single-PR diff; if asset size\n393\t  pushes the PR review out of bounds, prefer trimming the rendered feature set\n394\t  before adding a build pipeline.\n395\t\n396\t## Full 