licit command, not automatic interception\n583\t- resolves target paths/dirs\n584\t- gathers:\n585\t  - structural neighborhood\n586\t  - current hotspots\n587\t  - recent checkpoint intent/outcome summaries\n588\t  - relevant examples\n589\t- produces a bounded priming packet\n590\t\n591\tModes:\n592\t\n593\t- default: print/copy markdown or JSON packet for the user\n594\t- `--exec`: launch a **known Entire agent integration** selected by\n595\t  `--agent <name>`, prepending the priming packet where that agent's\n596\t  non-interactive interface supports it. The POC does **not** accept arbitrary\n597\t  free-form command strings after `--`; that would expand scope and bypass the\n598\t  repo's existing agent registry/capability checks.\n599\t\n600\t**POC `--exec` agent coverage (pinned):**\n601\t\n602\t- the POC ships `--exec` support for **claude-code** only, because its\n603\t  non-interactive CLI contract is already well-exercised by this repo's\n604\t  agent integration (`cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/`) and its E2E tests.\n605\t- other agents are accepted by name but produce a clear \"not yet supported\n606\t  for `--exec`; use the default packet output and pipe it manually\" message.\n607\t  Adding more agents is a follow-up and does not require schema changes.\n608\t- `--exec` defers all credential/auth handling to the underlying agent CLI;\n609\t  Entire only composes the prompt and invokes the known child integration.\n610\t\n611\tThis keeps priming explicit, inspectable, and reversible while still making the\n612\tfeature useful in daily work.\n613\t\n614\t## Dependency and verification guardrails\n615\t\n616\tDependency posture:\n617\t\n618\t- prefer **no new Go module dependencies** for the core engine; use stdlib plus\n619\t  existing repo dependencies unless a new package clearly removes substantial\n620\t  bespoke code\n621\t- do not add a Node build pipeline or npm workspace for the dashboard\n622\t- if the dashboard uses a third-party graph-rende