{"parentUuid":"c001ec4c-8600-43d6-9cbd-f3981ad2cf5d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HnRG9u63ekVdEduzQQjxfs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Start the dashboard server, then open the URL it prints. The server binds to `127.0.0.1` only and prints both the URL and the bearer token you'll need.\n\n**Step 1 — make sure the cache is built**\n\nThe dashboard reads from `.entire/understand/`, so build it first:\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/collab-95042499-claude\n./entire understand build --no-semantic\n```\n\n**Step 2 — launch the UI**\n\n```bash\n./entire understand dashboard --open\n```\n\nThat will:\n1. Pick a free port on `127.0.0.1`\n2. Print something like:\n   ```\n   dashboard: http://127.0.0.1:54321/\n     bearer token: REDACTED\n     press Ctrl-C to stop the server.\n   ```\n3. Open the URL in your default browser (because of `--open`)\n4. The HTML shell injects the bearer token into `window.__entireUnderstandToken` before the JS runs, so the page's `fetch()` calls authenticate automatically.\n\n`Ctrl-C` in the terminal stops the server.\n\n**If you don't want to open the browser automatically**\n\nDrop `--open`:\n\n```bash\n./entire understand dashboard\n```\n\nThen click/copy the printed URL yourself.\n\n**Curl the API directly (no browser)**\n\n```bash\n./entire understand dashboard --print   # prints would-launch-token (no server bound)\n```\n\nOr with a real server running, in another terminal:\n\n```bash\nTOKEN=<paste from server output>\nPORT=<paste port from server output>\ncurl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" http://127.0.0.1:$PORT/api/manifest | jq\ncurl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" http://127.0.0.1:$PORT/api/hotspots | jq\ncurl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" http://127.0.0.1:$PORT/api/timeline | jq\ncurl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" http://127.0.0.1:$PORT/api/checkpoint/<id> | jq\n```\n\nWithout the `Authorization` header you'll get `401 missing bearer token`. Putting the token in the URL (e.g. `?token=...`) is intentionally rejected — that's a deliberate spec contract.\n\n**Heads up on the UI itself**\n\nIt's deliberately plain (vanilla HTML over JSON, per the spec's \"no SPA framework, no design polish\" v1 cut). You'll see:\n\n- A pill row with build/structural/history/semantic status + node/edge counts\n- A Hotspots table (rows only when the repo has checkpoint history)\n- A Timeline table (one row per `introduced`/`modified` event)\n- An expandable `<details>` block with the raw fused graph JSON\n\nFor richer \"hover/click\" interaction in the UI, you'd want the follow-up PR per spec — v1 ships the auth contract and read-only endpoints as production-quality, with the visual layer intentionally minimal."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1890,"cache_read_input_tokens":544962,"output_tokens":1020,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1890,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1020,"cache_read_input_tokens":544962,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1890},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cak1DsohceV8i973EuYcQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"5338ce51-0284-4053-bd43-56de366eb6f9","timestamp":"2026-05-05T19:51:52.321Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/collab-95042499-claude","sessionId":"e4e10c4f-00ee-43dc-a2f3-a62030c8c6eb","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"collab/95042499/claude","slug":"peaceful-splashing-dijkstra"}
